---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import { href } from '../lib/paths';
import { roomMuseums } from '../lib/room';

const museums = (await getCollection('museums')).map((e) => e.data);
const items = (await getCollection('catalog')).map((e) => e.data);
const rooms = roomMuseums(museums, items);
const REPO = 'https://github.com/yusufaf/oil-on-cotton';
---

<Page
	title="About · Oil on Cotton"
	description="What Oil on Cotton lists, how its prices are checked, and who makes it."
	heading="About"
	lede="Oil on Cotton lists the clothing sold by museum shops. Each shop is a room, and every piece links to the shop that sells it. Nothing is sold here."
>
	<h2>What is listed</h2>
	<p>
		A shop gets a room once its terms have been read and they allow it. Rooms are open for {
			rooms.map((m, i) => (
				<>
					{i > 0 && (i === rooms.length - 1 ? ' and ' : ', ')}
					<a href={href(`rooms/${m.id}/`)}>{m.shop}</a>
				</>
			))
		}.
	</p>
	<p>
		Shops whose terms forbid collecting listings or prices, or forbid robots, are left out. The clause behind each
		decision is quoted in <a href={`${REPO}/blob/main/data/museums.yaml`}>data/museums.yaml</a>.
	</p>

	<h2>How prices are checked</h2>
	<p>
		A crawler called OilOnCottonBot reads each listed shop's clothing pages once a week. It signs its requests, follows
		robots.txt, and keeps only the name, price, sizes in stock and link of each piece. Its page is at <a
			href="https://bot.oiloncotton.com">bot.oiloncotton.com</a
		>.
	</p>
	<p>
		Prices and stock change between checks. Each room shows the date of its last check, and the shop's own page has the
		final word.
	</p>

	<h2>No money changes hands</h2>
	<p>
		The site has no ads, no affiliate links and nothing for sale. No shop pays to be listed, and the site earns nothing
		when you buy. It is not affiliated with or endorsed by any museum.
	</p>

	<h2>The walls</h2>
	<p>
		Each room is painted a colour from Robert Ridgway's <cite>Color Standards and Color Nomenclature</cite> (1912), and
		the colour's name is on the wall. For now the values are approximations from published ISCC-NBS centroids, not
		measured from the plates.
	</p>

	<h2>Who makes it</h2>
	<p>
		Made by <a href="https://yusufaf.dev">Yusuf Afzal</a>. The code is open source on <a href={REPO}>GitHub</a>. Write
		to <a href="mailto:hello@oiloncotton.com">hello@oiloncotton.com</a>, and see <a href={href('takedown/')}
			>Takedown</a
		> to have a piece or a shop removed.
	</p>
</Page>
